<title>JAPAN: Japan mine deal shows Chile's low risk -- diplomat.</title>
<headline>Japan mine deal shows Chile's low risk -- diplomat.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Japanese consortium's recent decision to take a large stake in a big Chilean copper mining project reflects the low risk of investing in the country, Chile's ambassador to Japan said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe the Japanese investors appreciated the low level of country risk in Chile,&quot; Jaime Lagos Erazo told a news briefing.</p>
<p>He said the Japanese had put up $400 to $500 million for their 40 percent stake in the Los Pelambres mine project, which is expected to produce 260,000 tonnes of contained copper per year when it is completed in 1999.</p>
<p>The five Japanese companies in the consortium are Nippon Mining and Metals Co, Mitsubishi Materials Corp, Mitsubishi Corp, Marubeni Corp and Mitsui &amp; Co.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
